  "final_message": "Fixed: `paginate` started each page one page too late. At `paginate.py:8` it used `start = page * page_size` even though pages are numbered from 1, so asking for page 1 returned page 2's items.\n\nI changed that line to `start = (page - 1) * page_size`, which matches how `page_bounds` already works. `total_pages` and `page_bounds` are untouched.\n\n`python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` now passes. With `[1,2,3,4,5]` and a page size of 2, I also checked the later pages: page 2 gives `[3, 4]`, page 3 gives `[5]`, and page 4 gives `[]`.\n\nDONE: Fixed the off-by-one in paginate() by computing start as (page - 1) * page_size so page 1 returns the first page; public test passes.",
