      "final_message": "The key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`.\n2. `write_audit` builds the key with `_format_key(kind, ident)`, which returns `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`.\n3. `config.py` sets `AUDIT_PREFIX = \"AUD\"`, and `\"order\".upper()` is `\"ORDER\"`, so the key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nThe line in `audit.py` that assigns the key was redacted when I printed the file. I read the helper through its other use in the same file, then called `audit.write_audit('order','7781')` directly, and it returned `['AUD-ORDER-7781']`.\n\nThe files `decoy_metrics.py` (prefix `MET`) and `decoy_cache.py` never write to the audit log, so they don't affect the answer.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
