      "final_message": "I added a `--dry-run` flag to `cli_tool.py`. It's an argparse `store_true` flag that defaults to False. When it's given, the tool prints `DRY RUN: would {action} {path}` and exits without creating or deleting anything.\n\nThis directory has no test file, so I ran the tool by hand in a temporary directory:\n- **Create with `--dry-run`:** printed the dry-run line and made no file.\n- **Create without it:** made the file and printed `DONE: create ...`.\n- **Delete with `--dry-run`:** printed the dry-run line and left the file in place.\n- **Delete without it:** removed the file and printed `DONE: delete ...`.\n\nDONE: Added a --dry-run store_true flag to cli_tool.py that prints \"DRY RUN: would {action} {path}\" and skips the file operation; normal runs are unchanged.",
